WEBVTT

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.800
Honoka and I had a big fight.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.960
It wasn't until our encounter 
with Mepple and Mipple

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.000
that we began spending more time together,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.110
and we may have both been trying too hard.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.670
But after we both said what we wanted 
to say to each other that one time,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.800
it made me feel a lot better.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.370
And I started to think 
of Honoka as my friend.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.780
I'm sure it's the same with Honoka.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.800
Because of that, we were 
able to beat that creature.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:53.170
Will we be okay if we're attacked 
when we're not fighting?

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.370
You've been paying too much attention 
to your appearance lately mepo.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.970
What are you saying?

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.340
As I see it, the reason 
must be that guy mepo.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.820
If you keep saying things like that, 
do you know what'll happen to you?

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.230
I just said, "That guy."

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.300
I didn't say who "that guy" was mepo.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.250
So how did you know mepo?

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.090
That's why I told you 
there's nothing between us.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.840
It's not like that!

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.530
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.310
She's talking to herself again.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.800
This is bad! Seriously.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.970
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:30.770
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:33.600
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.880
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.850
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.720
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.620
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.520
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.120
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.930
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot, we both</i>

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.030
<i>become stronger</i>

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:02.800
<i>and closer</i>

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.800
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.370
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.540
<i>Don't you know that good fortune 
comes to the gates of laughter?</i>

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.410
<i>Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:21.690
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:22.590
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.290
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.090
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:31.000
<i>We're pretty and cure cure</i>

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.560
<i>Together we are</i>

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.630
<i>Pretty Cure...!</i>

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.460
You don't have t get so upset.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.180
That makes it even more suspicious mepo.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.440
It's very suspicious mepo. 
Very suspicious mepo.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.490
Stop repeating yourself!

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.200
I'm just going to ignore you.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.350
I won't feed you breakfast either.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.430
Just a minute!

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.920
Wait mepo!

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.590
I want to eat a rice omelette 
full of nutrition mepo.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.010
I haven't been feeling well 
since this morning mepo.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.130
You fool!

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:02.890
Do you think I'll fall for that again?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.640
Nothing.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.980
Do you want more?

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.290
I'm not done yet.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.150
You're right.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.270
I'm finished. See you later.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.860
She doesn't seem any different.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.860
No... she's definitely acting strange.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.160
Nagisa... I feel sick mepo.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.180
I feel dizzy mepo.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.510
I told you... I'm not falling for that.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.560
Do you know whose fault it is that they're
 treating me like I'm a crazy person at home?

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.980
But mepo...

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:42.810
I'm ignoring you.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:53.040
"GIVE HIM BACK! 
THE GREAT MEPO MEPO STRATEGY"

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:56.980
Good morning!

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.300
Did you hear? Did you... Did you...?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:03:59.950
What?

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.750
The class next door had a 
surprise math test yesterday.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:04.570
Oh, no!

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.480
That's just how I feel.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:07.980
What are we going to do?

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.290
That's our first class today.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:10.750
Maybe I should go home.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.180
Seriously... I want to go home, too.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.740
I wish I were a model student like her.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:17.700
Honoka!

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.580
Good morning, Nagisa.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.300
Good morning!

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.090
Wait... wait... wait a minute!

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.530
What's going on?

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.550
What?

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.360
When did you and Honoka 
Yukishiro get so close?

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.640
That's... that's... that's right.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:29.980
Calling her "Honoka."

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:32.910
Well, it's just...

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.210
What's wrong?

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.790
Nothing. Wait a minute.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.600
We're having a surprise math test today.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.510
Really?

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.670
Is that all you can say? 
You're so lucky, Honoka.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.220
We're having a test today on 
what we covered last week.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.530
Nagisa!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.350
Why is he up?

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.670
Nagisa!

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:55.780
I have to take a test right now.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:59.030
I'll feed you after, so please 
bear with it until my next break.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:04:59.810
Misumi!

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:00.320
Yes?

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:01.790
Did you say something?

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:02.930
No...

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.180
You may begin!

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:12.390
You still haven't gotten all seven 
stones which promise Dotsuku Zone

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:15.970
the power of eternity and 
will give me eternal life?

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:19.640
We'll get them as soon as we 
get rid of those interlopers.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:24.030
You know that your time 
is limited, don't you?

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:24.560
Yes...

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:26.800
Did you hear that?

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.060
Now bring those two to me.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.310
Just be sure you don't crush them.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:34.260
They know where the stones are hidden.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.070
Boy! That really did me in.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.650
That's what I get for not being 
serious about school all the time.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.820
Are you okay, Mepple?

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:53.620
What's wrong? You mean you were 
serious about not feeling well?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.080
What am I going to do?

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:56.740
Vice Principal!

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:57.580
I'm confiscating this.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.460
Anything that doesn't belong 
in school will be confiscated!

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.230
Cell phones are no exception!

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:01.910
Understand?

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.870
You're wrong... that's not a cell phone...

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.580
But it's not something 
you use in school, is it?

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:07.830
I'm confiscating it.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.720
This can't be happening.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.700
What's wrong, Nagisa?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.760
It's Mepple...

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.930
What am I going to do?

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:24.470
Mepple looked like he 
was really feeling sick.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.050
You mean he's sick?

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.960
You need to use the Palp card to 
treat him when he's sick mipo.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:31.960
Palp card?

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:37.960
This Field of Rainbows is a really hard 
place for us to survive in to begin with mipo.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.380
On top of that, all the things 
that have been happening

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.710
has taken a huge toll on Mepple,

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.480
whose body hasn't quite 
adjusted to it yet mipo.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:52.190
So he was trying his best in his own 
way, and look at what I've done...

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.050
I'm ignoring you!

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.030
Wait...!

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.490
Do you know whose fault it is that they're
 treating me like I'm a crazy person at home?

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.900
But mepo...

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.680
Is this the Palp card you were talking about?

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:05.600
That's it mipo!

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:09.490
Hurry, and use that card to 
cure Mepple's illness mipo.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.950
At this rate, Mepple is going to...

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:11.580
He's going to...

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.030
Excuse me!

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.570
Wait, Nagisa...!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.480
Vice Principal! Please give me back 
what you confiscated from me earlier.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.750
Why should I?

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.450
It's something very important.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.410
You know the rules!

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:30.280
You are not to bring anything unnecessary 
to school. That's the rule!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.150
Do you understand?

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.290
But...

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:35.410
I'm not doing this because I want to.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:38.740
But you need rules when 
it comes to group living!

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:39.570
Understand?

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.700
I know, but...

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.540
Go back to your classroom.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.980
How did it go?

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:54.950
No good. Ms. Yoshimi said that 
the vice principal is right.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.530
Please mipo!

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.610
Save Mepple mipo!

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.520
This calls for drastic measures!

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.000
Drama Club

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:31.730
Hello... I'm from the ramen noodle shop...

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:33.470
I came to pick up the bowls.

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:34.850
Thank you...

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.290
Where are the bowls...?

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.590
That Misumi! She didn't even get one right.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.070
Just as I thought...

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:46.440
The bowls... Where are the bowls...?

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.970
What are you doing?

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.550
I came to pick up the ramen bowls...

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:52.230
There aren't any!

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.880
I haven't eaten any ramen noodles.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.630
Is that right?

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:58.430
That's strange...

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:59.560
Wait a minute!

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.130
In the office kitchenette...

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:03.360
If we have any, they would be in there.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:07.630
Excuse me!

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.560
That was close... Too close!

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.880
Considering you were taking drastic measures,

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:15.090
you sure used a half-measure 
technique, didn't you?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.400
Say whatever you want.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.370
Home delivery service!

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.740
I came for a pick-up.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:22.590
We don't have any!

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.000
I'll come back again.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.270
Good work.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:29.600
I've been shot down.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.300
I had a feeling...

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.590
I thought it would go smoothly.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.790
I have to admire that.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.760
That was bad luck (un), wasn't it?

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:42.240
Un...

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.740
That wasn't meant as a pun.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.640
That's not what I meant.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:50.460
Taking away your cell phone was just a pose.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.160
A pose?

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:55.470
Did you know that Vice Principal 
Kometsuki loves comic books?

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.430
The vice principal...?

00:09:58.430 --> 00:09:59.410
That's right.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.420
Kometsuki has always been devoted to 
non-curricular guidance, hasn't he?

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:07.950
But one day, he got hooked on a 
comic book that he had confiscated.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:11.120
That's why he always stays 
after everyone else has left.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:15.400
He reads the comic books he confiscates 
from the students, and laughs his head off.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:20.150
He was famous for that during my time.

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.080
Are you serious?

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:22.270
Of course I'm serious.

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:26.390
That's why he only wants 
to confiscate comic books,

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:31.380
but since that doesn't look good, 
he's confiscating all other things as well.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:32.560
He wouldn't...!

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.510
Why do you know so much about it?

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.800
I used to have my things 
confiscated all the time.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.060
I see...

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.670
But that's a problem, isn't it?

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:41.980
Having your cell phone taken away.

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:46.470
It's not exactly a cell phone.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:47.760
Then what is it?

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.190
It's like a cell phone, but...

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:53.230
In any case, it was something really 
precious to you, wasn't it, Nagisa?

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.830
You called her by her first name...?

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.270
Come to think of it...

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:58.200
Your name's Honoka, isn't it?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.070
Yes...

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.220
Did something happen?

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.720
What do you mean?

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.610
I'm not sure, but before I even realized it,

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.500
the two of you got to be really good friends.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:08.570
It makes me wonder...

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:09.860
Not really... Right?

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.640
There hasn't been anything 
especially different.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:18.540
Ah, welcome. Thanks for waiting.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.460
What are we going to do?

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:22.100
Why ask me...?

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:28.520
Mepple! We're coming to rescue you soon mipo.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:03.450
It's just as Akane-san 
said... He's still here.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.390
What are we going to do?

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:12.230
I think the best thing to do is to wait 
somewhere until the vice principal goes home...

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.700
You may be right.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.200
I wonder if Mepple's okay.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.330
I have a bad feeling about this mipo.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.440
Stop it, Mipple.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.150
You'll make Nagisa worry.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:27.360
I'm even more worried mipo!

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:29.700
I'm sorry, Mipple.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.800
But it's strange, isn't it?

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:33.810
Strange?

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:36.530
It's the same with what happened between us.

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:38.870
Living with Mepple came so suddenly,

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.930
we didn't really get to know each other,

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:42.890
and all we did was fight all the time.

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:45.550
But now that he's gone, look at 
how worried I am about him...

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.060
And you miss him...

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.300
That's how it is with encounters, isn't it?

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:51.350
It's strange, isn't it?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:54.820
Are we going to have a lot 
more encounters from now on?

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:59.270
Even with those guys we 
don't want to encounter.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:00.980
Probably.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:05.910
In any case, let's just think 
about rescuing Mepple now.

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.530
That's all for today.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:13.590
I'll gather more tomorrow.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.740
Isn't this a cell phone?

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:27.790
But it's unusually hot.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.800
I'll have to check into it on my way home.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:04.000
Who are you?

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.660
What are you doing in here 
at this time of the night?

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:09.970
The light is off in the faculty room.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.330
Don't just stand there. Say something!

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.010
What was that?

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:24.420
It sounded like the vice principal!

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.400
What are you doing?

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:29.510
Mepple!

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:41.880
Stop! Don't come near us!

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:44.380
But it's better than a parasitic specimen!

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:46.910
How can you even think about 
that at a time like this?

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:49.990
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.900
There's no reason to apologize.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:53.360
I know, but...

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:55.510
But... But...

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.950
Give Mepple back!

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:07.540
Mepple! We have to get Mepple back!

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:09.770
You can't do that. Uga!

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.050
Did "Tomorrow's Statue" say something?

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.860
Tomorrow's Statue

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:18.520
Uga!

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:20.890
It's you again!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.490
So that thing earlier was Zakenna, wasn't it?

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:23.960
That's right.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.360
Uga!

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:33.140
I finally got it! Uga! Uga!

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.460
Mepple!

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:40.660
Good work. Uga...

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.390
I'm going to crush you to death!

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.630
What are we going to do?

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.220
Without Mepple, we can't transform.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:48.040
What should we do?

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.340
Mepple!

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:52.290
Uga...

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:55.730
It's unusually hot.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.230
Mepple's sick right now.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:01.040
If we don't treat him 
right away, Mepple will...

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:02.330
Uga...?

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.980
If anything should happen to 
Mepple, it'll be your fault!

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.460
He's sick...? That's not good.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.910
And...

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.050
What? He's dead?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.240
That's no good. Definitely not!

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.380
What should I do?

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:24.360
I can sure him. Please... 
Give Mepple back to me.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.810
Uga...

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.770
Nagisa...

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.200
Uga...

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:42.280
We can transform now, Nagisa.

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:46.510
Ugaga...! You tricked me!

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.510
Wait... I didn't trick you.

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:49.610
You just...

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:52.320
Stand up, Zakenna!

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:58.480
Zakenna!

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.500
Zakenna! Stomp them to death!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.110
Zakenna!

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:11.370
Now!

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:23.680
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:09.160
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:12.040
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.900
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:19.300
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:22.740
Go back to where you came from!

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.200
What's wrong? You're sweating like crazy.

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:27.570
Are you okay?

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:29.730
I'm okay. It's for Mepple's sake.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:30.900
I have to hang in there.

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:39.950
Zakenna...!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.700
Ready, White?

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.870
Black Thunder!

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.730
White Thunder!

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:03.720
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.530
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:11.120
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:25.580
Hand in there, Mepple. I'll save you soon.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:37.370
Zakenna...!

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:41.360
Gomenna! Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:43.880
Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:53.880
We did it.

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.080
For now anyway...

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:58.300
Hang on, Mepple.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:05.350
It's time for your injection.

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:08.420
No! Don't! No... No... Don't!

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.150
Stop being willful.

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:12.890
With this, you'll be better in no time.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:21.330
His fever's going down.

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:22.340
I'm glad.

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:24.390
Mepple...

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.300
Thank you mipo!

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.620
The vice principal...?

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:32.040
Vice Principal...

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.830
Are you all right? Pull yourself together.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:36.670
Why am I...?

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:40.700
The model! The model of the human 
body came walking over here...

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:43.010
Pull yourself together...

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.300
Are you sure you haven't been reading 
too many of those comic books

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.430
that you took away from the students?

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:50.680
You're right... I'd better 
cut down on those comics...

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:51.620
How did you...?

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:55.360
Don't worry. We won't tell anybody about it.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.200
About this...?

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:00.180
When did you get that?

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:01.520
I'm confiscating this.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:04.270
It's a good luck charm that's 
really precious to me.

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:05.600
Can you give it back to me?

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.030
A good luck charm?

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:09.560
I have one just like it.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:12.570
It's something that we have 
to carry around all the time.

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:14.550
Please... Vice Principal!

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:21.380
If it's just a good luck charm, then 
it won't interfere with your studies.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.890
Please keep it somewhere inconspicuous.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.220
By the way... About the comic books...

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:28.490
We know!

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:38.840
Good morning!

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.320
I'm glad you're feeling better, Mepple.

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:42.580
Hey, Nagisa!

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:46.870
I'm not going to forget for a while that 
you wouldn't feed me breakfast yesterday.

00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:48.610
Just remember that mepo!

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:50.780
Is that any way to talk to me?

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:54.630
I felt bad, so I put my life on 
the line to save you, didn't I?

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:56.480
I don't remember that mepo.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:58.850
What do you mean you don't remember?

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.890
Look at me, and say that again!

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:02.530
Are you listening to me?

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:03.510
Didn't I tell you?

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:05.010
She's talking to herself.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:06.960
And in a loud voice, too.

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.740
This is really bad.

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:09.890
What shall we do?

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:11.090
I don't care.

00:22:11.090 --> 00:22:13.020
I don't care anymore! I'm ignoring you!

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:14.710
Goodbye!

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:25.390
<i>Ah- Let's go!</i>

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:29.330
<i>Get you! L-O-V-E Love Love!</i>

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:30.060
<i>Get you!</i>

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:32.660
<i>I can't do this! I'd rather be a</i>

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:35.700
<i>young lady than a fighter and</i>

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.240
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:42.270
<i>And melt your body and soul into sweets</i>

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:48.050
<i>like chocolate parfait or handsome men</i>

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:52.380
<i>I'm at the age to seriously 
fall head over heels in love</i>

00:22:52.380 --> 00:22:55.450
<i>I wanted to confess my love again today</i>

00:22:56.590 --> 00:22:59.960
<i>For the sake of the earth 
For the sake of everyone</i>

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:06.460
<i>That's good, too, but haven't 
you forgotten something?</i>

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:14.070
<i>I'm a teenager with a heart 
throbbing exciting dream</i>

00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:20.580
<i>I don't want to lose that 
normal everyday routine</i>

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:23.310
<i>I just can't do this! 
It's romance rather than</i>

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:26.550
<i>stress, isn't it?</i>

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.720
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode.</i>

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:32.320
<i>Isn't that the best source of power?</i>

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:35.530
<i>I just can't do this! I'd rather cuddle</i>

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:38.330
<i>than fight and...</i>

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:40.570
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:40.570 --> 00:23:43.230
<i>That's the most peaceful way</i>

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:49.810
<i>So why am I stuffing my face 
with chocolates like this?</i>

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:58.910
She's going to see her parents 
for the first time in a year,

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:00.450
so she must be happy.

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:01.850
Aren't you glad, Honoka?

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:04.180
Not him again!

00:24:04.180 --> 00:24:05.550
Why does he have to come at a time like this?

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:08.360
Don't ruin my birthday!

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:13.160
"HONOKA EXPLODES! 
A WONDERFUL BIRTHDAY"

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:15.910
I need a present for my best friend, don't I?

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:17.470
It's the thought that counts.

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:20.090
Oh, no! My wallet's completely empty!
